      "snippet": "#### Running the server\n\n```\n# Start full development environment\nmake dev-compose\n```\n\nThis starts the registry at\n```\nlocalhost:8080\n```\nwith PostgreSQL. The database uses ephemeral storage and is reset each time you restart the containers, ensuring a clean state for development and testing.\n\nBy default, the registry seeds from the production API with a filtered subset of servers (to keep startup fast). This ensures your local environment mirrors production behavior and all seed data passes validation. For offline development you can seed from a file without validation with\n```\nMCP_REGISTRY_SEED_FROM=data/seed.json MCP_REGISTRY_ENABLE_REGISTRY_VALIDATION=false make dev-compose\n```\n.\n\nThe setup can be configured with environment variables in docker-compose.yml - see .env.example for a reference.\n\nAlternative: Running a pre-built Docker image\nPre-built Docker images are automatically published to GitHub Container Registry:",
