      "snippet": "Memory MCP is a Model Context Protocol server that provides persistent semantic memory and knowledge graph capabilities for AI assistants. It solves the \"forgetfulness\" problem of AI assistants by enabling cross-session memory, semantic retrieval, and relationship tracking through a knowledge graph system.\n\n…\n\nFor Claude Desktop (\n\n`claude_desktop_config.json`):\n\n```\n\n\n\n\"mcpServers\": {\n\n\"memory\": {\n\n\"command\": \"node\",\n\n\"args\": [\"C:/path/to/mcp-memory/src/server.js\"],\n\n\"env\": {\n\n\"DATABASE_URL\": \"postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/mcp_memory\",\n\n\"DASHSCOPE_API_KEY\": \"sk-your-api-key\"\n\n\n\n```\nFor Windsurf (\n\n`mcp_config.json`):\n\n```\n\n\n\n\"mcpServers\": {\n\n\"memory\": {\n\n\"command\": \"node\",\n\n\"args\": [\"src/server.js\"],\n\n\"cwd\": \"C:/path/to/mcp-memory\",\n\n\"env\": {\n\n\"DATABASE_URL\": \"postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/mcp_memory\",\n\n\"DASHSCOPE_API_KEY\": \"sk-your-api-key\"\n\n\n\n```\nUse the\n\n`memory_create` tool to store information that should persist between conversations:\n\n```\n\n\n\n\"type\": \"preference\",\n\n\"content\": { \"topic\": \"programming languages\", \"preference\": \"likes Rust and Python\" },\n\n\"source\": \"user_message\",\n\n\"tags\": [\"programming\", \"preferences\"],\n\n\"confidence\": 0.95\n\n\n\n```\nRequired parameters:\n\n`type`: memory type (fact, preference, conversation, task)\n\n`content`: memory content (any JSON structure)\n\n`source`: origin of the memory (user_message, system_inference, external_api)\n\n`confidence`: certainty level (0.0-1.0)\n\nOptional:\n\n`tags`: array of tags for filtering\nUse\n\n`memory_search` for semantic retrieval:\n\n```\n\n\n\n\"query\": \"what programming languages does the user like\",\n\n\"type\": \"preference\",\n\n\"tags\": [\"programming\"],\n\n\"limit\": 5\n\n\n\n```\n\nThis tool converts your query text into a vector and finds semantically similar memories.\n\n`memory_update`: Update an existing memory (regenerates embedding if content changes)\n`memory_list`: List memories by type and tags\n\n`memory_delete`: Remove a memory by ID\n\nUse\n\n`graph_create_entities` to add nodes to the knowledge graph:\n\n```\n\n\n\n\"entities\": [\n\n\n\n\"name\": \"Memory MCP\",\n\n\"entityType\": \"Project\",\n\n\"observations\": [\n\n\"Uses PostgreSQL + pgvector\",\n\n\"Supports semantic search\",\n\n\"MIT license\"\n\n\n\n},\n\n\n\n\"name\": \"pgvector\",\n\n\"entityType\": \"Technology\",\n\n\"observations\": [\"PostgreSQL vector extension\", \"Supports HNSW indexing\"]\n\n\n\n```\nUse\n\n`graph_create_relations` to connect entities:\n\n```\n\n\n\n\"relations\": [\n\n\n\n\"from\": \"Memory MCP\",\n\n\"to\": \"pgvector\",\n\n\"relationType\": \"uses\"\n\n\n\n```\n\nThe system automatically creates bidirectional relationships (e.g., creating\n\n`A uses B` also creates\n\n`B is_used_by A`).\n`graph_add_observations`: Add new observations to existing entities\n\n`graph_search_nodes`: Find entities by semantic similarity or keyword\n\n`graph_open_nodes`: Get detailed information about specific entities\n\n`graph_read`: Retrieve the entire graph (suitable for small graphs)\n\n`graph_delete_*`: Various deletion operations\n\nKey configuration options:\n```\n\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@localhost:5432/mcp_memory\n\nDASHSCOPE_API_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n# Optional settings\n\nDB_MAX_POOL_SIZE=10\n\nSEARCH_DEFAULT_LIMIT=20\n\n```\n\nFull list of available environment variables:\n\n…\n\n|`SEARCH_DEFAULT_LIMIT`|No|`10`|Default search result limit|\n|`MCP_DEBUG_LOG_PATH`|No|`memory-debug.log`|Debug log path|\nTo add this MCP server to Claude Code, run this command in your terminal:\n\n`claude mcp add-json \"memory\" '{\"command\":\"node\",\"args\":[\"src/server.js\"],\"env\":{\"DATABASE_URL\":\"postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/mcp_memory\",\"DASHSCOPE_API_KEY\":\"sk-your-api-key\"}}'`\n\n…\n\n`~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`\n\n`%APPDATA%\\Claude\\claude_desktop_config.json`\n\n`~/.config/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`\n\n2. Add this to your configuration file:\n\n```\n\n\n\n\"mcpServers\": {\n\n\"memory\": {\n\n\"command\": \"node\",\n\n\"args\": [\n\n\"src/server.js\"\n\n],\n\n\"env\": {\n\n\"DATABASE_URL\": \"postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/mcp_memory\",\n\n\"DASHSCOPE_API_KEY\": \"sk-your-api-key\"\n\n\n\n```\n\n3. Restart Claude Desktop for the changes to take effect",
