      "snippet": "## 📋 Overview\n\nThis repo uses a set of\n```\n.mdc\n```\nrule files to ensure consistency, security, and best practices across all components. These rules were crafted to work seamlessly with AI IDEs that support custom rule configurations (like Cursor AI). We'll walk you through how to apply them, with tips for adapting to different IDEs.\n\n…\n\n### Step 1: Set Up Your AI IDE\n\nFirst, choose your AI IDE. We recommend Cursor AI (used to create these rules), but you can also use Windsurf or Bolt. Here’s how to configure the rules for each:\n- Cursor AI:\n  - Create a\n   ```\n  .cursor/rules\n  ```\n  directory in your project root.\n  - Copy all\n   ```\n  .mdc\n  ```\n  files into\n   ```\n  rules/\n  ```\n  .\n  - Cursor AI will automatically detect and apply these rules when you start coding.\n\n…\n\n#### 📜 mobile-rules.mdc (React Native)\n\n- Use Expo with Expo Router for navigation.\n- Style with NativeWind (consistent with TailwindCSS).\n- Use React Native Reusables for components.\n- Optimize with FlatList and React.memo.\n\n### Step 4: Configure Backend Rules\n\nRules for your NestJS backend.\n\n#### 📜 backend-rules.mdc\n\n- Organize code with NestJS modules.\n- Use DTOs with\n  ```\n  class-validator\n  ```\n  for input validation.\n- Implement RESTful API best practices.\n- Write integration tests with NestJS testing utilities.\n\n…\n\n### Step 10: Environment-Specific Rules\n\nRules for Dev, UAT, and Prod environments.\n\n#### 📜 dev-uat-rules.mdc\n\n- Use Groq AI for AI services.\n- Enable debug logging.\n- Test with real-world scenarios.\n\n#### 📜 prod-rules.mdc\n\n- Use OpenAI for AI services.\n- Disable debug logging.\n- Monitor usage for scaling.\n\n…\n\n#### 📜 checklist.mdc\n- Follow the Steps: Work through each section (e.g., Frontend Development, Backend Development) and check off tasks as you complete them.\n- Refer to Rules: Each checklist item links to a specific\n  ```\n  .mdc\n  ```\n  rule file for detailed instructions. For example, when setting up Next.js, refer to\n  ```\n  frontend-rules.mdc\n  ```\n  for App Router guidelines.\n\n…\n\n## ⚙️ Customizing Rules\n\nNeed to add project-specific rules? Use this template to create new\n```\n.mdc\n```\nfiles based on your Product Requirements Document (PRD):\nTemplate:\n```\nproject-specific-rules-{FEATURE_NAME}.mdc\n```\n```\nFilename: project-specific-rules-{FEATURE_NAME}.mdc\n---\ndescription: Rules for {FEATURE_NAME} based on PRD\nglobs: **/src/{FEATURE_PATH}/**,**/{FEATURE_FILES}**\nalwaysApply: {TRUE_FALSE}\n---\n\n- Implement {FEATURE_NAME} as per PRD requirements: {SPECIFIC_REQUIREMENTS}.\n- Use {SPECIFIC_FRAMEWORK_OR_LIBRARY} for {SPECIFIC_TASK}.\n- Define TypeScript types for {DATA_MODELS_OR_INTERFACES}.\n- Structure code: {SPECIFIC_STRUCTURE}.\n- Handle errors: {SPECIFIC_ERROR_HANDLING}.\n- Optimize for {PERFORMANCE_OR_SCALABILITY_CONCERN}.\n- Test {FEATURE_NAME} with {TESTING_APPROACH}.\n- Document {FEATURE_NAME} in {DOCUMENTATION_LOCATION}.\n\n```\nExample: For a \"User Profile\" feature:\n```\nFilename: project-specific-rules-user-profile.mdc\ndescription: Rules for User Profile Management based on PRD\nglobs: /src/app/profile/,/src/lib/profile/,**/*.tsx\nalwaysApply: true\nImplement User Profile Management as per PRD requirements: support profile updates, avatar uploads, and role-based views.\nUse React Query for fetching and mutating profile data.\nDefine TypeScript types for user profile data and API responses.\nStructure code: separate components, hooks, and API calls in src/app/profile.\nHandle errors: show user-friendly messages for failed updates, log errors to Vercel.\nOptimize for performance: use memoization for profile components.\nTest User Profile Management with React Testing Library for components and integration tests for API calls.\nDocument User Profile Management in src/app/profile/README.md.\n\n```\n\n…\n\n## 🌟 Next Steps\n\n1. Clone this repo into your project.\n2. Set up your AI IDE with the rules as described in Step 1.\n3. Follow the steps above to apply each\n   ```\n   .mdc\n   ```\n   file.\n4. Use the template to add project-specific rules.\n5. Deploy your app on Vercel and monitor with Prometheus!\n\n*💡 **Interactive Note**: Have questions? Open an issue in this repo, and I’ll help you out! Ready to build something awesome? Let’s get vibe coding! 🚀*",
