      "snippet": "# CursorRule - Customize Your Cursor AI Code Editor with Custom Rules\n\n## Master Custom Cursor Rules for Efficient Coding with Cursor AI\n\nLearn how to enhance your Cursor AI code editor with personalized Cursor Rules. Discover step-by-step tutorials, tips, and advanced configurations to improve your coding workflow.\n\n…\n\n### Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\n\n#### What is Cursor AI?\n\nCursor AI is a powerful code editor powered by artificial intelligence. It allows developers to enhance their coding experience by writing custom rules known as\n\n**Cursor Rules**, which help to automate coding tasks and improve efficiency.\n\n#### How do I create custom Cursor Rules?\n\nTo create custom\n\n**Cursor Rules**, you need to write specific instructions or prompts that tell the Cursor editor how to handle certain tasks. You can personalize your Cursor setup to fit your coding style by using these rules and improving your overall productivity.\n\n#### What is a Cursor Prompt?\n\nA\n\n**Cursor Prompt** is an instruction or a set of instructions that guide Cursor AI in performing specific actions. By utilizing Cursor Prompts, developers can automate repetitive coding tasks and focus on more complex work.\n\n#### Why should I use Cursor Rules?\n\nUsing\n\n**Cursor Rules** allows you to fully customize the Cursor AI editor to fit your unique coding requirements. By writing and applying these rules, you can streamline workflows, reduce manual input, and boost overall coding efficiency.",
