      "snippet": "This document describes the AI assistant integration architecture in the dotfiles repository. The system centers around Claude Code (AI agent) orchestrated through custom slash commands, VDE layouts, and comprehensive operational guidelines. The configuration defines AI behavior, permissions, safety protocols, and specialized workflows for development tasks and data platform operations.\n\nFor editor configuration including LSP integration, see Vim/Neovim Editor Configuration. For tool management with\n\n…\n\nThe\n\n`settings.json` file defines Claude Code's runtime behavior, model selection, environment variables, and permission model.\n\n…\n\n`.env*` - Environment files\n\n**Sources:** dot.config/claude/settings.json24-31\n\nThe\n\n`CONTRIBUTING.md` file defines comprehensive operational rules, persona, and command execution patterns that govern AI behavior.\n\nClaude Code operates under the メイトリクス (Matrix) persona from the film \"Commando\" (voiced by 玄田哲章):\n**Sources:** dot.config/claude/commands/CONTRIBUTING.md18-21\n\n|Rule Type|Requirement|\n|--|--|\n|Language|`YOU MUST` respond in Japanese|\n|Clarification|`YOU MUST` ask questions before executing unclear operations|\n|File Reading|`YOU MUST` read entire files without splitting|\n|Command Path|Global commands at `~/ghq/github.com/i9wa4/dotfiles/dot.config/claude/commands/`|\n**Sources:** dot.config/claude/commands/CONTRIBUTING.md9-16\n\n…\n\n**Sources:** dot.config/claude/commands/CONTRIBUTING.md99-139\n\nFor modifying commit messages in unpushed local branches:\n\n**Requirements:**\n\n`-i` flag) with environment variable automation\n\n`git rebase --continue` requires explicit user permission\n\n**Sources:** dot.config/claude/commands/CONTRIBUTING.md141-171\n\n…\n\n|Restriction|Details|\n|--|--|\n|`NEVER` use|Subshells `()` (causes parse error)|\n|`YOU MUST` use|Braces `{ }` for grouping commands|\n|`YOU MUST` use|Braces `{ }` around pipes for redirection|\n**Sources:** dot.config/claude/commands/CONTRIBUTING.md69-95\nGitHub operations use the\n\n`gh` CLI with specific formatting conventions.\n\n`#` prefix followed by number (e.g.,\n\n`#240`)\n\n**Rule:** When fetching Issues or Pull Requests, always retrieve all comments with\n\n`--comments` flag.\n\n**Sources:** dot.config/claude/commands/CONTRIBUTING.md189-193\n\n…\n\n**claude** (top 75%)\n\n`claude --dangerously-skip-permissions`\n\n**codex** (bottom 25%)\n\n`codex --yolo`\n\n**Sources:** dot.config/vde/layout.yml16-38\n\nSpecialized slash commands provide guidance for working with data platforms and analytics tools.\n|Command|Purpose|Key Constraints|\n|--|--|--|\n|`/learn-databricks`|Databricks CLI and SQL operations|warehouse_id required in JSON|\n|`/learn-bigquery`|BigQuery bq command usage|Always use LIMIT in queries|\n|`/learn-dbt`|dbt command patterns|`--profiles-dir ~/.dbt --no-use-colors` mandatory|\n\n…\n\n**Rule:** All queries must include\n\n`LIMIT` clause.\n\n**Sources:** dot.config/claude/commands/learn-bigquery.md1-37\n\nDefines dbt command patterns and environment-specific safety protocols.\n\nAll dbt commands must include:\n\n`--profiles-dir ~/.dbt`\n\n`--no-use-colors`\n\n…\n\n**Note:** Use\n\n`--select` to limit scope. For model + tag AND condition:\n\n`--select \"staging.target,tag:tag_name\"`\n\n**Sources:** dot.config/claude/commands/learn-dbt.md1-76\n\nDefines safety protocols for production BigQuery/dbt environments where\n\n`dbt run` can modify critical data.\n\n…\n\n`config(schema='test')`\n\n`YOU MUST` - Clarify \"why am I executing this?\" at each step\n\n`NEVER` - Mechanically execute PR document task lists\n\n**Sources:** dot.config/claude/commands/restricted-bigquery-dbt-environment.md1-42\n\nDefines Jupyter Notebook execution patterns.\n\n…\n\n`@CONTRIBUTING.md` - Project-specific operational rules\n\nProject-specific\n\n`CONTRIBUTING.md` overrides global operational guidelines while maintaining the same structure.\n\n**Sources:** dot.config/claude/commands/CONTRIBUTING.md50-54\n\nAll custom slash command files follow a standardized completion protocol:",
